{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Whatever has come to be</b>. Its name has already been called and it is known that it is man, thus and so. Why should one seek the going of the soul until he becomes like so-and-so — and perhaps he will not attain it? Nor is it fitting for a wise man to contend with one stronger than him. Therefore it is not fitting for him to seek what the living seek, and to do this against them, so that he will be like them."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:57.684231851Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}